4. The "Planet Hulk" Protocol
Source Material: Planet Hulk (2006)
The Narrative: The Illuminati (Iron Man, Dr. Strange, etc.) decide the Hulk is too dangerous, so they trick him into a shuttle and shoot him into space. They try to "externalize" their problem. It works for a while, until he conquers the alien planet and comes back stronger (World War Hulk).
The Business Translation: Externalities & "Offshoring" Risk.
 * D1 (Bio/Internal): The Exile
   * Logic: Trying to amputate a vital but volatile part of your organization (e.g., firing a "brilliant jerk" founder without fixing the culture).
   * Metric: Talent Retention / Cultural integration.
 * D2 (Tech/External): The Boomerang Effect
   * Logic: You cannot delete energy; you can only move it. The "waste" you ship away (e-waste, pollution, bad debt) eventually returns.
   * Metric: Supply Chain Circularity / Waste Management.
 * D3 (Eco/Resources): The Blowback
   * Logic: The "Problem" (Hulk) adapts to the new environment and weaponizes it against you.
   * Metric: Geopolitical Blowback / Litigation Risk.
 * D4 (Cosmic/Limit): Conservation of Energy
   * Logic: Every action has an equal and opposite reaction, often delayed by time.
   * Metric: Long-tail Risk Analysis.
